00:06:53,333 --> 00:06:59,333
Now More Than Ever!

2
00:13:46,666 --> 00:13:52,666
The Player is a mystery, drama, thriller film directed by Robert Altman.

3
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:46,000
A Hollywood studio executive is being sent death threats by a
writer whose script he rejected - but which one?

4
00:27:33,333 --> 00:27:39,333
Griffin Mill, played by Tim Robbins.

5
00:34:26,666 --> 00:34:32,666
June Gudmundsdottir, played by Greta Scacchi.

6
00:41:20,000 --> 00:41:26,000
Walter Stuckel, played by Fred Ward.

7
00:48:13,333 --> 00:48:19,333
Detective Avery, played by Whoopi Goldberg.

8
00:55:06,666 --> 00:55:12,666
Larry Levy, played by Peter Gallagher.

9
01:02:00,000 --> 01:02:06,000
Joel Levison, played by Brion James.

10
01:08:53,333 --> 01:08:59,333
The Player is a 1992 American satirical black comedy mystery film directed by
Robert Altman and written by Michael Tolkin, based on his 1988 novel.

11
01:15:46,666 --> 01:15:52,666
The film stars Tim Robbins, Greta Scacchi, Fred Ward, Whoopi Goldberg, Peter Gallagher, Brion James and Cynthia Stevenson, and is the
story of a Hollywood film studio executive who kills an aspiring screenwriter he believes is sending him death threats.

12
01:22:40,000 --> 01:22:46,000
The Player has many film references and Hollywood in-jokes, with 65
celebrities making cameo appearances in the film.

13
01:29:33,333 --> 01:29:39,333
Altman once stated that the film "is a very mild satire," offending no one.

14
01:36:26,666 --> 01:36:32,666
The film received three nominations at the 65th Academy Awards: Best
Director, Best Adapted Screenplay and Best Editing.

15
01:43:20,000 --> 01:43:26,000
The film also won two Golden Globes, Best Motion Picture – Comedy or
Musical and Best Actor – Comedy or Musical for Robbins.

16
01:50:13,333 --> 01:50:19,333
The film explores themes of based on novel or book,
homicide, movie business, blackmail, screenwriter.

17
01:57:06,666 --> 01:57:12,666
The tone is intense and lighthearted and emotional.
